WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.500
Fyana!

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.000
Chirico?!

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:49.630
Non-aggression Zone

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.920
What's the enemy's strength?

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.170
Attack team one's final report
said there were two ATs.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.750
And those two ATs took out
all forty units of the attack team?!

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.750
Yes, sir.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.750
A ship of no clear nationality...

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.460
with two absolutely incredible ATs defending it.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:17.920
They may be good in a fight,
but they can't defeat the second attack team.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.210
Every human being has to
reach his limit eventually.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.130
If we keep pressing the attack-

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.790
We aren't dealing with normal humans.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.130
What do you mean, Captain?

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.960
I have no doubts now. Those are PSs.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.960
Although HQ still has its doubts.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.460
They've completed a Perfect Soldier?!

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.040
But, that's...!

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.130
The situation is clear to see!

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:47.250
Do you think there's a normal pilot
who can maneuver an AT like that?!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.830
Maybe the ship's from
some world in Balarant space.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.080
If it is, then our problem is a small one.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.880
If it's from Gilgamesh space,
then it's a damned sight bigger.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.630
Definitely.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.630
So, some nation put those PSs
on that ship to battle test them?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:06.170
Yes. Well, seeing how they've violated
Galactic Law, we're justified in attacking them.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.830
We have to capture a PS.
That's the key to this mystery.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.750
That man...

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.290
That was me...

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.670
That was me, when...

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.380
Chirico!

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.920
Chirico!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.130
Chirico!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.460
One enemy AT seems to have taken damage.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.170
Keep up the attack!

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:28.080
Use any means necessary
to capture those two PSs!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.580
Aye, sir! I'll give the order.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.420
I'm getting worried about
where that ship's headed.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:35.250
They may be in contact with others in their group.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.080
The ship's running on autopilot.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.130
Take out their engines and stop them!

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.130
Sir!

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.960
Keep up the attack!

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.630
We'll be able to capture the PSs
if we destroy their ATs!

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.040
And take out that ship's autopilot system!

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:48.790
Sir!

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.920
Chirico, you're still badly hurt.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.420
Please, just lie still.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.460
I was born to fight.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.500
And I'm a PS, meaning I was made to fight.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.750
I'm a butcher.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.210
I have to fight... till I die.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.670
Don't say that.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.380
Go! Just go!

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.170
Forget about me!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.290
Chirico!

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.040
You're burning up... Stay here!

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.880
Chirico, I won't let you die.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:00.670
I won't let you.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.710
It's getting ready to land on that planet!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.710
We just have two ATs to deal with here. Find them!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.380
You're still here?

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.080
Fyana, surrender.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.880
The Balarant will accept you.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.670
Be quiet. You aren't helping yourself.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.710
That doesn't matter.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.960
What's so funny, Chirico?

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.500
I was just thinking. About Ypsilon.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:38.250
He'd never abandon you.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.880
I know he's coming. Coming for you...

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.960
Stop it, Chirico!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.380
I-

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.460
Pathetic, aren't I?

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.960
Nobody...

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.790
...could ever love me.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.630
Hey! There she is!

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.330
Uh-oh!

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:37.790
An AT!

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:38.710
Shoot!

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:39.830
Dunno if this'll work.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:43.040
Their control systems aren't anything like ours.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.330
As long as it takes out their autopilot system!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.460
Did you get her?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.080
Nah, got away. Let's go!

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:09.380
She's unarmed. Capture her alive!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.250
They've entered the Nonaggression Zone,
as we expected.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.460
This is control. Report commencing.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:55.580
Current position: X-135°, Y-38.46°, Z-38.38°.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.250
Captain!
Current position: X-135°, Y-38.46°, Z-38.38°.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.580
We have to recall the second attack team!

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.830
What are you saying?!
There are PSs on that ship!

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.880
If we let this chance slip away, they'll-

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.540
And you'd violate the cease-fire for that?!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.830
They broke it first! Captain!

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:40.670
There she is!

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.630
They just issued the recall order!
Return to the ship!

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.380
Why?! We almost have her!

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.210
Move it! This is an emergency!

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:56.380
Yes, sir!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.380
The PSs are at our fingertips!

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.040
We'll hide our ship's nationality.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.380
All transmissions are to be
scrambled from now on.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:29.920
Just keep track of that ship's position.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:30.630
Yes, sir!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:41.960
What's on the planet this ship is headed for?

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.580
And what will we do when it gets there?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.170
Who's in control of this ship?

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.540
My fate is in someone else's hands.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.580
Who's leading us on like this?

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.960
I have a feeling I'll get my answer soon.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.580
I sense them near.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.790
The roar of cannons.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.380
The deep crimson of blood.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.960
And the awful stench of death.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:20.670
You could match me when you were in an AT.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:24.920
But a true warrior must win
in all forms of combat!

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.380
Do you understand, Chirico?!

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:41.880
Chirico!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.420
Chirico!

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:13.080
Ypsilon, don't move.
We have to run these tests.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:17.670
If you don't stop fidgeting,
the data will be useless.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:25.170
Look, the wave form's being disrupted again.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.460
Now, look-

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.500
Looks like we should leave him alone for now.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:32.500
Oh yes.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.880
The rise in the R-ratio of the Noytron B
could cause trouble.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.880
The Balarant ship Leslion transmitted
a second position report.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.460
After that, they made a transmission
without a nationality ID code.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.460
They must be worried about being
inside the Nonaggression Zone.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:59.500
The real question is that ship Chirico's on.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.710
Where the devil did it come from?

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.210
Test time, Ypsilon.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.710
Come along. Be a good boy.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.790
Preparations: okay.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:29.210
All right, let's begin.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.130
Fyana!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.540
You called me "Fyana."

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:53.630
Is that a name you've given me?

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.170
I wanted to call out to you.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.540
Even though your coming to see me again
meant having this happen...

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.130
I'm glad you're here.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.750
If you come with me,
we'll make it out, somehow.

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:08.130
I want to go with you, but right now...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.580
Fyana!

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.080
I'm glad.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.040
Fyana!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.000
I'm glad.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.500
I want to go... with you.

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:18.630
Fyana!

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.080
This is communications section.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:32.330
The unidentified ship is at
X-135°, Y-38.46°, Z-38.2°.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.420
Ship has entered the Nonaggression Zone.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.580
Repeat, the unidentified ship...

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:37.880
Well?

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.880
Looks good. This imagination tape
we made from Proto One

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:45.000
is producing very high levels of excitement data.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:50.500
If we can amplify his hatred for Chirico,
we'll have perfected the PS.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.920
Looks like Borough's idea wasn't wrong after all.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.630
We have to be careful in the
Nonaggression Zone...

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.460
what with that ship and
the Balarant being here.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:03.670
Why should that matter?

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.920
Galactic Law is meaningless to us.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.630
No, we have to hide our existence
from both sides.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:11.960
We can't allow anyone else to know that PSs exist.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:17.000
True, but our objective here is
the eradication of Chirico Cuvie.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.420
And of Proto One as well.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:23.460
We have to erase all knowledge of the PS.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:25.330
Let's head them off.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.880
Our current position puts us at
an advantage over the Leslion.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.790
I know.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.130
But why are Chirico and Proto One on that ship?!

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:35.210
Maybe they stole it from somewhere.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.750
How? Even if they were both PSs...!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.290
I don't know.

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.290
Could another organization
we don't know about be involved?

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:46.670
A mystery... And the solution may lie
in the Nonaggression Zone!

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:49.500
Anyway, let's get after that ship.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.540
Time for a jijirium shower.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.290
Jijirium density: 0.012

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.670
Immersion time: 8 minutes, 30 seconds.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.630
Okay. End time: 3 seconds.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.540
Because I love him!

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:27.000
Stop it, Ypsilon!

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:29.920
Stop it!

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:34.130
Ypsilon!

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.290
This is radar section.

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.420
We've picked up the unidentified ship.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:55.040
The Balarant ship behind us has
launched a small vessel in pursuit.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:00.670
Captain, the Balarant seem to have detected us.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.330
Forget them.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:04.540
They're just one more non-aligned ship out here.

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:33.420
Chirico, I won't let you die.

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:36.880
I've wandered the depths of Hell.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:41.040
Its hot, suffocating depths...

00:22:41.790 --> 00:22:43.790
And in the distance, a light!

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:49.830
Our ship, as though following
a beckoning beacon in the night

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:52.830
drew ever closer to the planet that lay before us.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:59.170
People ask why. And they get answers.

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:04.330
But, so often, the answer they get
isn't to the question they asked.

00:23:04.790 --> 00:23:07.710
Questions are swords. Answers are shields.

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:10.130
Sparks fly as they clash endlessly.

00:23:10.130 --> 00:23:14.420
And the truth is often hidden in the shadows
thrown in the instant they hit.

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:16.750
Next time, "Ypsilon"

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:21.790
The starving always ask questions,
and in the answers lie traps.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Ypsilon

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
